<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#intercession-of-the-theotokos">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Intercession of the Theotokos</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pokrov</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Intercession of the Theotokos (Pokrov) is an Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> feast, celebrated on 1 October (14 October in the Gregorian calendar), commemorating a vision of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mary-mother-of-jesus">Virgin Mary</a> spreading her veil over the faithful in the Blachernae church in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. Though based on a Byzantine story, the feast was established in Rus', traditionally by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrei-bogolyubsky">Andrei Bogolyubsky</a> in the twelfth century, and became one of the most important in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/intercession-of-the-theotokos.jpg" alt="Intercession of the Theotokos" width="320" height="378" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Icon_02041_Pokrov._Ikona._XIX_v._Rossiya.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
